# Internet Mood Map — Example Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you need.
# The MVP works fully on mock data, so every variable below is OPTIONAL
# right now. Later phases will start to read these values.
#
# IMPORTANT: never commit real keys. `.env*` files are gitignored.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 2 — Data source mode
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects how the /api/mood route builds its response.
#   mock            -> bundled mock data, no random drift (deterministic)
#   live-simulation -> bundled mock data + small random drift (default, matches MVP)
#   hybrid          -> try real signals, blend with mock, fall back on failure
#   real            -> only real signals (falls back to live-simulation on failure)
#
# Can also be overridden per request via the ?mode=... query param on /api/mood.
# Unknown values silently fall back to "live-simulation".
# MOOD_DATA_MODE=live-simulation

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 4 — Optional real data sources
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of RSS / Atom feed URLs to ingest. When empty, the
# RSS adapter reports itself as unavailable and the orchestrator falls
# back to live-simulation with a warning in the API response.
#
# Feeds are fetched server-side only, each with a ~6 second timeout. The
# total number of signals returned per request is capped at 50.
#
# Examples of safe, free, public feeds (NO API key required):
#   - BBC World:        http://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/world/rss.xml
#   - Reuters World:    https://www.reutersagency.com/feed/?best-topics=world&post_type=best
#   - Al Jazeera:       https://www.aljazeera.com/xml/rss/all.xml
#   - NPR World News:   https://feeds.npr.org/1004/rss.xml
#
# RSS_FEED_URLS=

# GDELT is a public global events dataset and does not require a key.
# Leaving this blank disables GDELT ingestion.
# GDELT_QUERY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 5 — Optional Supabase / Postgres database (via Prisma)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pooled connection string used at runtime.
# DATABASE_URL=
# Direct (non-pooled) connection string used by Prisma migrations.
# DIRECT_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 7 — Optional AI-generated explanations
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provide exactly one of the following keys to enable AI explanations.
# If both are missing, the app falls back to rule-based text.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
